 Connecticut.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John C. Hadjipateras | Chairman of the Board, President & CEO | Age 75 | Compensation: $3.4M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 602 people. Revenue per employee of $800K ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers, with revenue growing 15%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $18K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Dorian LPG Ltd. is a small-cap energy business with a $1.9B market cap on $482M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 7.2\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 14% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 4.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (92% sell ratio, net $7.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"